/* The file defines both P and P_neg, and P_neg negates P.  P holds
   everywhere (every x reaches 5 counting up), so P_neg 3 is 3 < 0 \/ not
   (P 3), which is false.  The dual drawn for the negation of P must not
   take the name P_neg, which the input already defines. */
P_neg 3
s.t.
P (x: int) : bool =mu x >= 5 \/ P (x + 1);
P_neg (x: int) : bool =mu x < 0 \/ not (P x);
